  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\n## COLLEGE CONTACTS Years 7-12\n\nTelephone:  9208 2500 Facsimile:   9271 9663 Uniform Shop:  9208 2690 Canteen:  9208 2565 www.chisholm.wa.edu.au admin@chisholm.wa.edu.\n\nau\n\nOffice Hours: 8.15am 4.30pm P O Box 89 Inglewood\n\n6932\n\n## OUR WEEKEND PARISH MASSES\n\n## BALLAJURA\n\nMary MacKillop Catholic Com-\n\nmunity\n\nSaturday 6pm,\n\nSunday 8am, 9.30am &amp; 5pm\n\n## BASSENDEAN\n\n## ST JOSEPH'S\n\nSaturday 6.30pm Sunday 7am &amp; 9am\n\n## BAYSWATER\n\nSt Columba's\n\nSaturday 6pm\n\nSunday 7.30am &amp; 9.30am\n\nYouth: Last Saturday of the\n\nmonth 6pm\n\nBEDFORD\n\nSt Peter's\n\nSaturday 6pm, Sunday 8.30am\n\n&amp; 10am\n\n## DIANELLA\n\nOur Lady's Assumption Saturday 6.30pm\n\nSunday 7.30am &amp; 9.30am\n\n## EMBLETON\n\nHoly Trinity\n\nSaturday 6pm, Sunday 9am\n\n&amp; Aboriginal Mass at 11am\n\n## HIGHGATE\n\nSacred Heart\n\nSaturday 6pm\n\nSunday 9am &amp; 10.15am (Italian)\n\n## LOCKRIDGE\n\nGood Shepherd\n\nSaturday 6.30pm\n\nSunday 8am, 9.30am &amp; 5pm\n\n## MAYLANDS\n\nQueen of Martyrs\n\nSaturday 6pm, Sunday 9.30am\n\n&amp; 7pm\n\n## MORLEY\n\nInfant Jesus Saturday 6.30pm Sunday 7.30am &amp; 9.30am 11.30am (Italian) &amp; 6pm Youth: 2nd &amp; 4th Sundays 6pm\n\n## CANTEEN ROSTER FOR WEEK COMMENCING Monday 25th October 2010\n\n| Mon 25th               | Tue 26th                 | Wed 27th                | Thu 28th             | Fri 29th                                         |\n|------------------------|--------------------------|-------------------------|----------------------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| M White  9.15am-1.30pm | S Washbourne  9am-1.30pm | C Smith  8.30am-11.30am | L Pinner  9am-1.30pm | D Audino  8.30am-11am  R Nocciolino  10.30am-2pm |\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nOn Monday 18 th October, approximately 500 members of our Chisholm community gathered to acknowledge some of the wonderful team and individual sporting performances for 2010.  Special guests Ms Shae Bolton (West Coast Fever Netball) and\n\nMr Trent Mitton (Kookaburras gold medalist at the recent Delhi Commonwealth Games) shared the night with our future sporting stars.  Both were able to offer some advice and inspiration for all who attended.\n\nTrent with Lara Ameduri and Danika Vidakovich\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nCongratulations to all our award winners and in particular\n\nJustin Skowron who was awarded the 'Peter Tonkin' award for the most outstanding Year 12 sports person.\n\nWell done to all of you.\n\nMr Andrew Glover, Head of Sport\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n## STUDENT CONGRATULATIONS William Edge Year 11Laurence1\n\nWilliam has been selected to represent WA in the upcoming All Australian Basketball Tour to USA. He will participate in several competitions on the West Coast of America and play against some of the best USA College Basketball Teams. The tour takes in LA, San Diego, Las Vegas and Phoenix and will last from 28 th Nov to 23 rd Dec. Well done William and good luck for the Tour. We are very proud of you.\n\n## HAVE YOUR SAY ON PUBLIC TRANSPORT IN YOUR LOCAL COMMUNITY ADVANCING PERTH'S EASTERN REGION\n\nSeven Public Transport Forums are being held across the region during October and November 2010. These forums aim to engage and encourage the community to become more aware of the vision for increased public transport and the options and delivery modes that exist. You can register by contacting Samantha Robshaw on email samantha.robshaw@emrc.org.au",
